1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:06,420
Hey everyone! This is our submission for the Flip the Switch Hackathon in Track 1:

2
00:00:06,420 --> 00:00:08,140
Best Business Workflow.

3
00:00:08,140 --> 00:00:13,100
Solo AI coding agents in terminals are great, but when a critical P0 outage strikes at 3:00 AM...

4
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:19,900
...engineering is collaborative. Fragmented alerts across Datadog, GitHub, and Slack cause chaos.

5
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:24,150
We built SwitchOps to bring agents directly into team chat.

6
00:00:24,650 --> 00:00:32,550
Using open-source Switch, we transformed Slack channel #incidents-production into a shared room.

7
00:00:32,550 --> 00:00:38,970
Notice how human teammates Priya, Sam, and Alex share the room with three specialized agents:

8
00:00:38,970 --> 00:00:44,650
@SwitchTriager, @InfraOps, and @HotfixCoder.

9
00:00:44,650 --> 00:00:51,000
They all read from the exact same shared memory, tasks, and decision log.

10
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:54,960
Sam reports checkout API 500 errors.

11
00:00:54,960 --> 00:01:00,900
Instantly, @SwitchTriager analyzes the logs and flags Postgres connection pool exhaustion.

12
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:09,440
Then @InfraOps inspects recent deployments, pinpoints the faulty commit in release v2.14.0...

13
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:13,450
...and prepares our rollback manifest to version v2.13.2.

14
00:01:13,950 --> 00:01:20,790
Because Switch strictly enforces Rule-01, agents cannot touch production without human sign-off.

15
00:01:20,790 --> 00:01:27,970
Priya taps her Wispr Flow key and dictates: 'Approved. Roll back cart-service to version v2.13.2.'

16
00:01:27,970 --> 00:01:33,950
Wispr Flow transcribes it 4 times faster than typing, and Switch records the cryptographic...

17
00:01:33,950 --> 00:01:36,900
...hash in the immutable Decisions Log.

18
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:45,320
@HotfixCoder executes the rollback, connection pool drops from 100% to 14%, latency...

19
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:51,260
...drops back to 48ms, and the blameless post-mortem is automatically synthesized.

20
00:01:51,260 --> 00:01:56,860
SwitchOps turns solo agents into your team's most dependable production allies.

21
00:01:56,860 --> 00:01:59,850
Thank you WeMakeDevs and Switch!
